// selection.proto — WHICH TESTS A RUN RUNS, named down to the single subtest.
//
// A selection names tests by WHERE THEY LIVE (a Go package's directory, a test
// file, a harness script) and, within that, by their own names, never by
// suite or by unit: the runner (testrun) resolves each target to the roster
// suite that owns it and builds only the units that run what was named, with
// the build and program units they need. A target no suite owns, or a test
// name the target does not define, is refused rather than run as nothing.
//
// THE NARROWEST RUN IS THE DEFAULT ONE TO ASK FOR. An agent names exactly the
// tests its change touches; the whole roster is the merge queue's to run.
//
// Every path is RELATIVE TO THE REPOSITORY ROOT (for example
// "modules/app/agent-repl/daemon/internal/merge"), so a selection reads the
// same from every directory and names one place.

